## 1. What pypods is

- A single Python file, `pypods.py`, with one dependency: `pynput` (`pip install pynput`). Python 3.8 or newer.
- It turns the three buttons on headphones (volume up, volume down, play/pause) into game inputs named `plus`, `minus` and `middle`.
- It gives you a game loop: you subclass `Game` and fill in `setup`, `update(dt)`, `draw` and `teardown`.
- It detects gestures: press, release, tap, double tap and long press.
- It draws text in the terminal without flicker (`self.show(text)`).
- Normal keyboard keys work too, so every game can be played and tested without headphones.
- The input listener is system-wide: keys are heard even when the terminal or game window is not focused.

