## 10. Common mistakes

| Wrong | Right |
|---|---|
| Writing `__init__` | Put start-up code in `setup()` |
| `if self.action_held("jump"): jump()` | `action_pressed`: `held` jumps every frame |
| `pressed` for single action **and** `double_tapped` on the same button | Use `tapped` for the single action |
| `self.x += 5` | `self.x += 300 * dt` |
| `print()` inside `update`/`draw` | `self.show(...)` |
| Calling `setup()` to restart | Write and call `reset()` |
| Registering callbacks in `update()` | Register once in `setup()` |
| `time.sleep()` or `input()` in the loop | Timers with `dt` |
| Only headphone buttons in `controls` | Add keyboard keys to every action |
| Requiring `NEXT` / `PREV` | Optional extras only |
| Binding `"-"` or `"="` to a different action | They already mean `minus` / `plus` |
| `on_action("jump", self.jump)` (function in the event slot) | `on_action("jump", fn=self.jump)` |
| Logging pressed keys to a file | Never store keystrokes |
| Inventing an API like `self.text()` | Only use section 5 |

